main.cpp
--cpp23
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ if consteval: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[stmt.if]/4: the first substatement of `if consteval' is executed in an
immediate function context or during manifestly constant evaluation.  The
parser kept only the else branch, so the constant evaluation of
`constexpr int c = f()' took it too (c was 2).  Both branches are now kept
(cpp23_if_consteval_forms).
